===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|ota|شایقه|tr=şayka}}, from {{der|ru|bg|ша́йка|t=saic|id=saic}}. {{doublet|ru|ча́йка}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ша́йка}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ша́йка|*}}

# {{lb|ru|historical}} {{C|ru|Watercraft}} [[saic]], a kind of small [[boat]] of up to twelve [[cannon]]s heavily used in the [[Black Sea]], [[Tisa]], [[Danube]] and [[Sava]]; similar to the {{l|ru|ушку́й}} used in {{w|Republic of Novgorod|Novgorod}}
# {{C|ru|Containers}} [[washtub]], [[tub]], [[pail]]
#: {{syn|ru|бадья́}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1836|author=w:ru:Александр Пушкин|title=w:ru:Капитанская дочка|chapter=[[s:ru:Капитанская_дочка_(Пушкин)/1960_(СО)/Глава_III|Глава III. Крепость]]|location=London|publisher=Henry S. King & Co.|newversion=English translation from|translator2=Ekaterina Telfer|title2=The Captain's Daughter|location2=|publisher2=|year2=1875|page2=|pageurl2=|text=— Все, слава богу, тихо, — отвечал казак, — только капрал Прохоров подрался в бане с Устиньей Негулиной за '''шайку''' горячей воды.|t="All's correct, God be praised," answered the Cossack, quietly; "only Corporal Próhoroff has had a fight with Oustynya Pezoulin in the bath house about a '''pail''' of hot water."}}
# {{C|ru|Collectives|Crime}} [[gang]] of [[rogue]]s, [[band]] of [[bandit]]s (originally: [[sea]]-[[raider]]s on [[saic]]s, like [[ushkuinik]]s)
#: {{syn|ru|ба́нда|вата́га}}

